ision pending user: denkhaus-lab ahead 52 (revisor results merge), denkhaus ahead 2 (engine seeds).","labels":["needs-triage"],"closedAt":"2026-09-03T17:30:40.873Z","closeReason":"Grilling concluded 2026-09-03: all six round-1 questions answered (Q1 validation pass, Q2+Q9 supersession, Q3 engine seed fabro-9588, Q4 efforts kept, Q5/Q7 caps removed, Q6 engine seed fabro-017f after finding the mandate already existed unenforced). Implemented: revisor graph+prompts 385dc03cb, label backfill 55 seeds, ADR-0014, glossary on meta. Remaining: start validation pass."}
-{"id":"fabro-93f2","title":"gofib: add -step <int> flag printing every step-th number of the selected range","status":"in_progress","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T21:03:56.493Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T21:07:19.978Z","description":"Today gofib prints every Fibonacci number in the selected range (-n/-start/-limit). Add a -step flag (default 1) that strides the selection: with -step k, only every k-th number of the selected range prints, in every output mode (text, json, pretty, table, csv).\n\nRules: -step must be >= 1 (invalid values exit non-zero with a stderr message naming the flag and the rule, like -n); -step 1 behaves exactly as today; a positive -seed keeps single-index semantics and ignores -step (not an error); -sum sums the numbers that remain AFTER stepping.\n\nAcceptance: (1) gofib -n 6 -step 2 prints 3 numbers (first, third, fifth of the six); (2) -step 0 and -step -2 exit non-zero with a stderr line naming the flag; (3) -step 2 -json emits JSON Lines with exactly the stepped indices; (4) unit tests cover stride selection, validation errors, and the -seed interaction; (5) just qualitygate stays green."}
