 {"id":"fabro-87cf","title":"gofib: add -last <int> flag printing only the last k numbers of the selected range","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T21:03:56.580Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T21:03:56.580Z","description":"Add -last k (default 0 = unset) to print only the LAST k numbers of the selected range, in every output mode.\n\nRules: k must be >= 1 when set (invalid values exit non-zero with a stderr message naming the flag); if the selection has fewer than k numbers, print all of them (clamp, not an error); combination order is selection (-n/-start/-limit) then -step stride then -last tail (document the order in the flag help text); a positive -seed overrides everything single-index style and conflicts with -last like it conflicts with -sum (exit non-zero, stderr names both flags).\n\nAcceptance: (1) gofib -n 10 -last 3 prints the 3 highest indices of the default sequence; (2) gofib -n 2 -last 5 prints both numbers (clamp); (3) -last 0 behaves as today; (4) -last -1 exits non-zero with stderr naming the flag; (5) -last 2 -step 2 takes the last 2 of the stepped selection; (6) unit tests cover tail selection, clamping, validation, ordering with -step, and the -seed conflict; (7) just qualitygate stays green."}
